## What this package changes

This app **does not patch** DSH's source code. It packages DSH as-is and adds host
integration plus a small shell plugin that wraps the existing DOM:

1. Ships a fixed Node.js runtime (official Linux x64 build, MIT) so TOS does not need Node preinstalled
2. Ships the DSH npm release package `@deepseek-ai/dsh` (MIT) and its production dependencies
3. Seeds a DSH profile; at install time it generates the `pageHosts` config from the local IP/hostname
4. Ships the open-source plugin `@he0119/dsh-tailnet-admin` (MIT), used to disable the
   browser session check so the reverse-proxied page works
5. Provides the systemd unit, nginx reverse-proxy config, install/uninstall scripts and documentation
6. Since 1.1.0, ships the local voice runtime `sherpa-onnx-linux-x64` (Apache-2.0) plus
   SenseVoice `tokens.txt` / Silero VAD, and enables voice input in the profile; the
   239 MB recognition model is still downloaded by DSH on first use
7. The Office preview component `@deepseek-ai/libreoffice-kit-wasm` is installed on demand
   (see README)
8. Ships the sidebar shell plugin `@surpasshither/dsh-shell-ui` (MIT): UI-only workspace
   categories, blue running indicators and a mobile-app entry point. It does not modify
   DSH's source and only wraps the existing DOM.
9. A planned mobile app (separate package) will add local login and TOTP in front of DSH;
   this package does not include it and does not modify DSH's source

